  "uuid": "06c8a76f-1712-41e9-a0b6-2ceb284ec79f",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "fc9c47e7-34c3-88c1-665e-ec7fc10692d1",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "3cb14c49-15ab-da22-09aa-e4d6fefa3287",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The chief guest, Professor Mohammad Khurshid, Medical Director, Aga Khan University Hospital and Associate Dean Clinical Affairs, AKU, appreciated the efforts of the Society in creating awareness on infection control methods. He went on to encourage the Society to initiate training programmes in this field for health care personnel. Dr Hasan Nawab, President, ICSP, said that educational videos on topics such as hand washing and hepatitis as well as a health magazine, \"Jahan-I-Sehat\", were taking the lead in educating the public. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Amongst the other international speakers, Dr Paul Rooney, Consultant Microbiologist, Belfast City Hospital, Northern Island, noted the preventive aspects of T.B. He supported sputum tests for T.B diagnosis as the most cost effective, especially in diagnosing lung T.B that is a major source of the spread of infection. He also stressed the need to formulate a reliable local T.B prevention policy. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Nizam Damani, Consultant Microbiologist and Medical Director, Craigvo Area Hospital, U.K, spoke on precautionary measures against the spread of infection in a hospital setting. He said that the use of brooms for sweeping hospital floors increases the bacterial count by 700 percent. He also advocated the use of disposable syringes for injections in all hospitals. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Raymond Smego, Professor and Chairman, Department of Medicine, AKU, highlighted the prevention strategies for various blood borne diseases. Dr Wasim Jafri, associate Professor, Department of Medicine, AKU, focused on the prevention of Hepatitis Band C viruses as a major cause of chronic liver diseases in the country. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Prof Ali Muhammad Ansari, Professor of Orthopaedics and Ex-Director General Health, spoke on the risk of surgical infections and highlighted preventive aspects for reducing that risk.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
